# This repo is PUBLIC (github.com/cwill713/Movie-Catalog).
# Strategy: ignore everything at the repo root, then explicitly allow what we track.
/*

# --- Tracked at root --------------------------------------------------------
!.gitignore
!/README.md
!/requirements.txt
!/pytest.ini
!/.env.example
!/app/
!/scripts/
!/migrations/
!/tests/

# --- docs/: split between this public repo and a private one -----------------
# SPEC.md and WORKLOG.md carry personal detail and conversational context, so
# they are NOT published here. They live in a separate private repository
# (docs/ is its own git repo with its own remote), which also backs them up.
#
# DECISIONS.md and ARCHITECTURE.md are written free of personal data and are
# published from this repo. tests/test_decisions_doc.py enforces that.
/docs/
!/docs/
/docs/*
!/docs/DECISIONS.md
!/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md

# --- Secrets: never track ---------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
/API_KEYS.txt

# --- IMDb non-commercial datasets -------------------------------------------
# Licensed for personal, non-commercial use only. Redistribution is prohibited,
# and this repository is public. The dumps and anything derived from them must
# never be committed. We commit scripts/ingest_imdb.py, never the data.
/data/
*.tsv
*.tsv.gz

# --- TLS certificates -------------------------------------------------------
# Local dev certs from mkcert. The .key file is a PRIVATE KEY; publishing one
# lets anyone impersonate this host to a browser trusting the local CA. The
# root-level /* rule already covers /certs/, but say it explicitly too - this is
# a public repo and defence in depth costs nothing here.
/certs/
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.pfx

# --- Databases --------------------------------------------------------------
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# --- Python runtime ---------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
